{"repo": {"timestamp": 1786031657000, "version": 20002, "name": "Alisher's apps", "icon": "icon.png", "address": "https://xalisher.github.io/fdroid/repo", "description": "Private, self-hosted Android apps on Logos \u2014 no Google, no accounts, no central server. Peers: a peer-to-peer messenger over Logos, MeshCore (LoRa) and Bluetooth mesh, end-to-end and at-rest encrypted. Booth & Receiver: broadcast and tune in to decentralised anonymous radio over Tor + Logos Messaging."}, "requests": {"install": [], "uninstall": []}, "apps": [{"authorName": "xAlisher", "categories": ["Internet", "Multimedia"], "suggestedVersionCode": "1", "description": "Broadcast a decentralised, anonymous radio station from your phone: create a\nstation, speak into the mic, and listeners tune in over Tor + Logos Messaging.\n\nThree-phase flow (Setup \u2192 Staging \u2192 Live) with a live-status dashboard, a\nreal-time mic waveform, mute, and identity tiers: Anon, on-device key, or a\nhardware Keycard over NFC. The broadcasting mirror of Receiver.", "issueTracker": "https://github.com/xAlisher/booth-android/issues", "license": "MIT", "name": "Booth", "sourceCode": "https://github.com/xAlisher/booth-android", "summary": "Broadcast a decentralised anonymous radio station", "added": 1783356066000, "packageName": "com.boothandroid", "lastUpdated": 1783356066000}, {"authorName": "xAlisher", "categories": ["Internet"], "suggestedVersionCode": "113", "description": "A private, peer-to-peer messenger. Your identity lives on this device \u2014 no phone\nnumber, no account, no central server, no Google.\n\nReach people over three transports: Logos (a pure-Rust delivery node), MeshCore\n(LoRa radio), or Bluetooth mesh \u2014 one shared timeline, colour-coded by transport.\n1:1 and group chats are end-to-end encrypted with MLS; send voice notes, images,\ncamera photos, and location. Works offline over Bluetooth/LoRa when the network\nis down.\n\nYour messages, encryption keys, and identity are encrypted 